        "id": "tool:score-held-out-lines-with-a-small-model",
        "label": "Measure how well a small model judges my rules on lines it never trained on (runs on your computer)",
        "job": "Check how well my trained model catches lines that break each of my rules",
        "description": "Scores the held-out test lines, the never-trained lines and the held-out set with a decider model, with or without a LoRA adapter, and reports per law: AUC of the probability of the failing answer on bad vs good lines, recall at the thresholds that fail 1%, 2% and 5% of good lines, the same with only written good lines, the share of other laws' bad lines it also fails, the held-out set's good lines failed (by kind) and bad lines caught, and each never-trained line's verdict. A line is scored per sentence and takes its highest probability. Given scores_from, it reports again from an earlier run's kept scores without a model. Fit the lines a gate uses with tool:fit-pass-and-fail-lines.",
        "status": "active",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
