              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "description": "[scope_kind, scope_id]: which row to read when settings_record holds several."
            }
          },
          "description": "With settings_record, the person's score settings give the keys the request leaves out (all but the paths)."
        },
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "Summary lines, then a last line {\"result\": {results_file, asks, seconds, laws: {<law>: {n_bad, n_good, auc, recall_at_2pct}}}} or {\"error\": \"what to change\"}. The results file holds per law the report (auc, at_1pct/at_2pct/at_5pct, written_good, other_law_bad_flagged_at_2pct, film: the held-out set, narrator: the never-train lines, top_good, missed_bad) and scores {test, narrator, film} it was made from."
        },
